 r←SubmitToIndexNow(url key);u;c;q;resp;endpoint
⍝ Announces a single URL to IndexNow and returns the HTTP status, or 0 when nothing came
⍝ back. Submitting to one participating search engine shares it with the others, so one
⍝ request per URL is all that is wanted.
⍝ 200 and 202 both mean accepted - 202 says the key is still being checked. Anything else is
⍝ logged: a 403 means the key file cannot be read back, which is worth knowing about because
⍝ nothing else would ever show it.
 r←0
 endpoint←'https://api.indexnow.org/indexnow?url=',(R.PercentEncode url),'&key=',key
 :Trap 345                                          ⍝ Rumba turns every failed connection into 345
     u←R.ParseURI endpoint
     c←R.NewClient endpoint
     c.CongaTimeout←3000
     c.ClientTimeout←10
     q←R.NewRequest u.Resource
     resp←⊃c R.SendAndReceive q
 :Else
     :Return                                        ⍝ Unreachable; the next publish tries again
 :EndTrap
 r←resp.StatusCode
 :If ~r∊200 202
     LogError'IndexNow refused "',url,'" with status ',⍕r
 :EndIf
⍝Done
